; Move the story-window cursor back one character
;
; The story window packs 42 characters of 6 pixels into 32 cells, so a character
; starts at pixel offset C (0-7) inside a cell. Subtracts GLYPH_WIDTH from C;
; when that goes below 0, adds 8 and moves to the cell on the left.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; C Pixel offset of the character inside its cell, 0-7
; HL Screen address of the cell
; O:C New pixel offset
; O:L Low byte of the cell address, one less when C wrapped
@label=StepCursorBack
c$8761 LD A,C
@isub=SUB GLYPH_WIDTH
 $8762 SUB $06
 $8764 LD C,A
 $8765 RET NC
 $8766 ADD A,$08        ; borrow: 8 pixels per cell
 $8768 LD C,A
 $8769 DEC L
 $876A RET
